config CHOPIN_CRUMB
	bool "Chopin early-boot breadcrumbs"
	help
	  Record early boot progress into the pstore block at 0x48090000 so
	  it is carried into the expdb partition on the next start. Used to
	  locate where the 4.19 kernel stops, since UART output is muted by
	  LK and no in-kernel dump path exists on this tree.

	  Each stage stores a small record through the identity map (before
	  setup_arch()) or the linear map (after it) and cleans it to the
	  point of coherency, so the value survives into DRAM where LK's
	  kedump exports it.

	  Say N if you do not need boot breadcrumbs on Chopin.
